{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather to Me seventy men of the elders of Israel, whom you know, that they are the elders of the people and its officers.</b> Whom you know that they are the elders of the people and its officers who were struck over the public in Egypt at the hands of the taskmasters, who were Egyptian; and these officers would have compassion on them and lighten from them the yoke of labor, and they would be beaten on that account by the taskmasters, as it says (Exodus 5): ״ויכו שוטרי בני ישראל״ — for they know how to lead the people and to bear them." "<b>And it appears</b> that even though it says now 'Gather to Me,' Israel already had seventy elders in Egypt, for from the time they went down to Egypt, seventy souls, and the blessing spread in their seed, they appointed over them seventy elders to lead them and to teach them righteous statutes and laws, for they were great sages, receivers of the tradition of the fathers, and they knew that the seventy souls were a model, and therefore they appointed over them in Egypt seventy elders. And so it is written (Exodus 3): ״לך ואספת את זקני ישראל״ — and they were seventy; and they were present at the giving of the Torah, as it is written (Exodus 24): ״ויעל משה ואהרן נדב ואביהוא ושבעים מזקני ישראל״. And what it mentions here, 'Gather to Me seventy men,' these were others who were chosen now anew, for those seventy elders of the giving of the Torah died in the burning, for they were worthy of the emissary from Sinai, and therefore it was necessary to say that he should gather them anew; and he gathered them by means of slips, as the Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned. And what it says, 'whom you know, that they are the elders of the people' — that is, among them should be those officers who were in Egypt, who were beaten over the public. And from the day they went down to Egypt, seventy souls, this number never ceased from Israel, not in the wilderness, not in the First Temple, nor in the Second." "<b>And know</b> that there were seventy elders and Moshe above them, and with him they were 71, in the pattern of the seventy princes above, who are the princes of the seventy nations, and the Holy One, blessed be He, is supreme over all of them, and with Him they are 71; and in this number were those who went down to Egypt, and the household of Yaakov was 71; also the Sanhedrin in the Holy Temple were seventy, and they are called the Great Sanhedrin, and with the Nasi who is over them they are 71." "<b>And you will find</b> in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer: the Holy One, blessed be He, said to the seventy angels who surround the throne of His glory, Come and let us confound their language — and they are the very court of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said of Him: ״וה' בכל מקום הוא ובית דינו״." "<b>From now on</b> understand the verse that says (Exodus 1): ״ואלה שמות בני ישראל הבאים מצרימה את יעקב״ — they are seventy souls from the power of Yaakov; and corresponding to 'each man and his household' (איש וביתו) they came, for the intention in it is: he and his court (בית דינו) came; and there I wrote that the Great Name, the Explicit Name — its numerical value and its letter-spelling is 71; and so you will find the appellation Alef-Dalet, which is the attribute of judgment — it is 71 when it is spelled with a Vav, so as to include Him and His court. And so it is written (Amos 7): ״והנה אדוני נצב על חומת אנך״. And Scripture says: ״ויעמד אותם סביבות האהל״ — that Moshe, peace be upon him, stationed the seventy elders around the Tent, just as the Holy One, blessed be He, stationed seventy angels around the Throne of Glory." "<b>And now.</b> See, yes see, the greatness of Moses: for the prophecy of the seventy elders was drawn from the power of Moses, just as the forces of the seventy angels are emanated from the power of the Holy One, blessed be He. This is the meaning of ״ויעמד אותם סביבות האהל״ — and He caused them to stand round about the Tent — for the Ark that is in the Tent is a likeness of the Throne of Glory, as I have written in the section of ויקחו לי תרומה." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״אספה לי״ — Gather to Me. We find thirteen things specially designated for the Holy One, blessed be He, and they are: silver and gold, the priests, the Levites, Israel, the firstborn, the altar, the terumah, the anointing oil, the Tent of Meeting, the kingdom of the house of David, the offerings, the land of Israel, and the elders. Silver and gold, as it is written (Haggai 2:8): ״לי הכסף ולי הזהב״. The priests, as it is written (Exodus 29:1): ״לקדש אותם לכהן לי״. The Levites, as it is written (Numbers 3:12): ״והיו לי הלוים״. Israel, as it is written (Leviticus 25:55): ״כי לי בני ישראל עבדים״. The firstborn, as it is written (Numbers 8:17): ״כי לי כל בכור״. The altar, as it is written (Exodus 20:21): ״מזבח אדמה תעשה לי״. The terumah (Exodus 25:2): ״וקחו לי תרומה״. The anointing oil (Exodus 30:25): ״שמן משחת קדש יהיה זה לי״. The Tent of Meeting (Exodus 25:8): ״ועשו לי מקדש״. The offerings (Numbers 28:2): ״להקריב לי״. The kingdom of the house of David (I Samuel 16:1): ״כי ראיתי בבניו לי מלך״. The land of Israel (Leviticus 25:23): ״כי לי הארץ״. The elders (Numbers 11:16): ״אספה לי״. This is what the verse says (Amos 9:6): ״הבונה בשמים מעלותיו ואגודתו על ארץ יסדה״ — To what may the matter be compared? To a palanquin built upon the deck of a ship: as long as the planks of the ship are joined together, that which stands upon it stands. So too, ״הבונה בשמים מעלותיו״ — He who builds His upper chambers in heaven — for the sake of Israel, when do they have standing? When ״ואגודתו על ארץ יסדה״ — and His band is founded upon earth. And thus it says (Deuteronomy 33:5): ״ויהי בישרון מלך בהתאסף ראשי עם״. This is what the verse says (Ecclesiastes 12:11): ״דברי חכמים כדרבונות״ — The words of the wise are as goads. Just as this goad teaches the cow to plow and to straighten the furrows, so the words of the wise direct their learners to declare of the forbidden, 'forbidden,' and of the permitted, 'permitted,' and they show rulings and instructions from the Torah, as it is said (Proverbs 22:17): ״הט אזנך ושמע דברי חכמים״. And three names were given to it: דרבן (goad) — that it teaches [from the root מרדע]; דרבן — that it directs (דר) understanding to the cow; מלמד (teacher) — that it teaches her to plow; מרדע (goad) — that it imparts knowledge (מורה דעה) to the cow." "<b>And in the chapter.</b> In tractate Hagigah, chapter 1: ״דברי חכמים כדרבונות״ — why were the words of Torah compared to a goad? Just as this goad directs the cow to its furrows to bring life to the world, so the words of Torah direct the heart of the learner from the ways of death to the ways of life. If you say: just as this goad is movable, so the words of Torah are movable — Scripture says: ״וכמשמרות״ (and as fastened nails). If you say: just as this nail diminishes and does not increase, that is, it wears away over the length of time, so the words of Torah diminish and do not increase — Scripture says: ״נטועים״ (planted). Just as this planting produces and multiplies, so the words of Torah produce and multiply. ״וכמשמרות נטועים״ — from here the Sages said: it is forbidden to read in the external books, for it is written ״נטועים״, and just as the priestly watches are twenty-four thousand, so the books worthy of being planted are twenty-four; therefore it is written ״וכמשמרות״ with a shin. ״בעלי אסופות״ — these are the Sanhedrin, for it is written ״אספה לי״. Lest you say: behold, this one forbids and that one permits, this one disqualifies and that one declares fit, this one declares impure and that one declares pure — how do I learn Torah from now on? — all of them were spoken by one Shepherd, as it is said (Ecclesiastes 12:11): ״נתנו מרועה אחד״. And the intention is that all the precise details of the commandments are in the language of the verse."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {4 "Comment 1: 'בתבערה' (in the burning) likely refers to those consumed at Taberah (Numbers 11:3), though the identification of the original seventy elders as perishing there is Rabbeinu Bahya's own tradition; rendered hyper-literally. Comment 4: the phrase 'בוא״ו' means 'with a vav,' referring to the full spelling אדוני (with vav) versus the defective spelling אדני (without vav); the vav is needed to reach the count 71.", 6 "Source citations given as book name + chapter only; verse references normalized where identifiable. For מלכות בית דוד the source reads 'ביד דוד' which has been rendered faithfully as written.", 7 "Header reads 'ובמסכת חגיגה פ״ק' rendered as 'And in the chapter, in tractate Hagigah, chapter 1.' The reading that priestly watches (משמרות כהנים) number כ״ד אלף (24,000) follows the text as written; this figure appears in b. Hagigah 3a in connection with the number of books, though some witnesses there read differently."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:48.927068934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}